Description: Fix Enyo 2 apps on webOS 2.1.0 (V8 compiler bug)
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "Title":"V8 Fix for webOS 2.1.0", "FullDescription":"Makes Enyo 2 apps such as Preware 2 display and work on webOS 2.1.0.<br><br>The JavaScript engine in webOS 2.1.0 has a code generation bug that breaks minified Enyo 2 (the app opens but its screens stay blank or broken). This package switches the engine that runs apps to its full code generator, which does not have the bug, by adding --always_full_compiler to the JavaScript flags in /etc/palm/browser.conf. Before changing anything it tests the device for the bug and does nothing if the bug is not there. The web browser is not changed.<br><br>Restart Luna after installing or removing. Removing the package takes the flag out again.", "MinWebOSVersion":"2.0.0", "MaxWebOSVersion":"2.1.9", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartLuna", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartLuna", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna" }
